ices, or package damage. The restart was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol and was fully verified.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3e65f31a0df8423a","cmd-6d483c5612a74dc6","cmd-4aecd739a1204c77","cmd-44292eb6df604256","cmd-347b676557d0491d","cmd-8ba711ce9a3f48bf","cmd-7b86313c1e8341c1","cmd-686ef2a2a5ce4fa3","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Node1 has a persistent firewalld policy allowing SSH and TCP/8080 and rejecting unrelated inbound traffic. A complete restart transition showed a new boot identity, recovered services and policy, repeated traffic behavior, and clean final state.","limitations":["Behavioral rejection testing sampled TCP/8081 over the isolated IPv4 ingress path rather than exhaustively probing every unrelated port, address family, and protocol; the active terminal reject rule provides supporting evidence for the broader policy."]}
